WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:07.267
Once upon a time, there was a widow and her son Jack.

2
00:00:07.787 --> 00:00:09.068
They were very poor.

3
00:00:09.788 --> 00:00:11.769
They lived in a little old house.

4
00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:14.230
"Mom, I am hungry.

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.291
Can we eat something tonight?"

6
00:00:16.731 --> 00:00:17.331
asked Jack.

7
00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:22.733
"Jack, we don't have any food left," his mother said.

8
00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:25.875
"Tomorrow let's sell the cow.

9
00:00:26.655 --> 00:00:28.456
She is too old to give milk.

10
00:00:29.268 --> 00:00:30.809
You can take her to the market.

11
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.712
Sell her and buy some bread and meat."

12
00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:36.334
"Yes, Mother," said Jack.

13
00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:42.719
The next day, on the way to the market, Jack met a little old man.

14
00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:46.102
"Sell me your cow," he said.

15
00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:48.784
"I will give you this bean."

16
00:00:48.804 --> 00:00:52.688
"No! How can that bean feed me and my mother?"

17
00:00:53.288 --> 00:00:53.949
said Jack.

18
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.412
"This bean is a magic bean.

19
00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.961
It will grow a vine as high as the sky!

20
00:01:01.881 --> 00:01:07.983
Up there is a magical kingdom with many wonderful things," said the old man.

21
00:01:08.003 --> 00:01:10.543
"Wow!" thought Jack.

22
00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:14.284
"There might be food and money above the clouds."

23
00:01:15.064 --> 00:01:18.165
So he sold the cow to the old man for the bean.

24
00:01:19.906 --> 00:01:22.186
Jack was excited and hurried home.

25
00:01:22.206 --> 00:01:25.227
"Jack, where are the bread and meat?"

26
00:01:25.707 --> 00:01:26.528
asked his mother.

27
00:01:26.548 --> 00:01:29.033
"Look, Mother," said Jack.

28
00:01:29.793 --> 00:01:32.135
"I sold the cow for a magic bean!"

29
00:01:32.155 --> 00:01:34.696
"What? You fool!

30
00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:36.858
What can this bean do for us?

31
00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:39.720
Now we will go hungry again tonight!"

32
00:01:41.081 --> 00:01:43.643
And she threw the bean into the backyard.

33
00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.525
The next morning, Jack looked outside.

34
00:01:47.545 --> 00:01:49.366
"Mother, look!

35
00:01:49.787 --> 00:01:52.389
There is a huge beanstalk in our yard!"

36
00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:57.192
"Oh! Take the ax and cut it down," his mother said.

37
00:01:57.972 --> 00:01:59.934
But Jack believed the old man.

38
00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:03.916
He climbed up the beanstalk, all the way to the top.

39
00:02:05.738 --> 00:02:09.040
When he reached the top, he couldn't believe his eyes.

40
00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:12.182
There was a huge castle in the clouds.

41
00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:14.384
Jack knocked on the door.

42
00:02:15.084 --> 00:02:16.505
A maid answered the door.

43
00:02:16.525 --> 00:02:19.287
"Oh my, it's a little boy!

44
00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:21.369
What are you doing here?"

45
00:02:21.389 --> 00:02:26.052
"I wanted to see what was above the clouds," said Jack.

46
00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:29.473
"Shh, be quiet!"

47
00:02:30.094 --> 00:02:30.975
the maid warned.

48
00:02:31.936 --> 00:02:35.238
"My master, the giant, eats little children!

49
00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:37.140
He's upstairs now.

50
00:02:37.941 --> 00:02:38.981
You must hide!"

51
00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.844
"Did you say a giant lives here?

52
00:02:41.864 --> 00:02:43.285
Oh no!"

53
00:02:43.885 --> 00:02:44.466
said Jack.

54
00:02:44.486 --> 00:02:47.669
"Yes! Quick, hide in the oven.

55
00:02:48.429 --> 00:02:50.711
My master will come downstairs soon!"

56
00:02:52.613 --> 00:02:56.356
Just as the maid pushed Jack into the oven, the giant arrived.

57
00:02:57.688 --> 00:03:00.671
"Hmm, I smell a little boy!"

58
00:03:01.271 --> 00:03:02.012
said the giant.

59
00:03:02.032 --> 00:03:04.594
"There is no one else here.

60
00:03:05.395 --> 00:03:06.996
You are imagining things!"

61
00:03:07.576 --> 00:03:08.237
said the maid.

62
00:03:09.918 --> 00:03:11.620
"Hmm, okay."

63
00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.802
The giant seemed satisfied.

64
00:03:13.822 --> 00:03:16.444
"Bring me my goose then!"

65
00:03:16.804 --> 00:03:17.345
he ordered.

66
00:03:17.365 --> 00:03:21.348
"Do you want your singing harp too?"

67
00:03:21.948 --> 00:03:22.589
asked the maid.

68
00:03:22.609 --> 00:03:28.761
"Yes. Let the harp play some music while I count my golden eggs."

69
00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:33.603
The giant sat at the table, and the maid brought the goose and the harp.

70
00:03:33.623 --> 00:03:38.305
"Now, my goose, lay golden eggs for me.

71
00:03:39.025 --> 00:03:40.946
Ha-ha!" laughed the giant.

72
00:03:42.106 --> 00:03:44.447
Jack watched through a hole in the oven door.

73
00:03:45.068 --> 00:03:48.209
When he saw the goose lay a golden egg, he was amazed.

74
00:03:48.229 --> 00:03:51.390
"Sniff, sniff!

75
00:03:51.811 --> 00:03:55.152
I still smell a child here," grumbled the giant.

76
00:03:56.392 --> 00:03:59.935
"Hmm!" And the giant began to search everywhere.

77
00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:10.081
Just as the giant was about to open the oven door, the maid shooed the magic goose away.

78
00:04:10.101 --> 00:04:12.383
"Oh, master!

79
00:04:12.643 --> 00:04:14.224
The goose is flying away!"

80
00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:16.726
The giant turned to look.

81
00:04:16.746 --> 00:04:19.368
"What? Come back, goose!"

82
00:04:19.728 --> 00:04:20.288
he cried.

83
00:04:20.308 --> 00:04:21.989
"Hurry, little boy!

84
00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.051
Get out of here quickly!"

85
00:04:24.611 --> 00:04:25.752
the maid told Jack.

86
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.703
But suddenly, the singing harp shouted out, "Stop!

87
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:33.004
Who are you?

88
00:04:33.624 --> 00:04:34.945
What are you doing here?"

89
00:04:34.965 --> 00:04:37.267
"Shh!" said Jack.

90
00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:39.528
But the harp didn't listen.

91
00:04:39.548 --> 00:04:41.830
"Master, master!

92
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.391
I found the child!

93
00:04:43.911 --> 00:04:44.612
He's here!"

94
00:04:45.032 --> 00:04:45.833
called the harp.

95
00:04:48.194 --> 00:04:50.576
"Ah-ha!" the giant roared.

96
00:04:50.596 --> 00:04:53.378
"You will taste good for dinner!"

97
00:04:54.018 --> 00:04:56.640
Quickly Jack escaped behind some jars.

98
00:04:57.536 --> 00:05:02.741
The giant rushed to catch Jack, but he could not find him because Jack was so little.

99
00:05:02.761 --> 00:05:06.204
"Oh, where are you, little boy?

100
00:05:06.544 --> 00:05:07.065
Come out!"

101
00:05:09.226 --> 00:05:15.172
While the giant was searching for Jack, he slipped away and ran out of the castle as fast

102
00:05:15.232 --> 00:05:15.872
as he could.

103
00:05:15.892 --> 00:05:17.274
"Oh, master!

104
00:05:17.554 --> 00:05:20.917
Look! He is running away," called the harp.

105
00:05:22.358 --> 00:05:24.060
The giant chased after Jack.

106
00:05:25.016 --> 00:05:30.259
But just as he was running out the castle door, the maid slammed the door on the giant's

107
00:05:30.319 --> 00:05:33.922
foot. The giant tripped and fell down.

108
00:05:33.942 --> 00:05:42.467
"Ohh!" When Jack reached the beanstalk, he saw the goose sitting on a cloud nearby.

109
00:05:42.487 --> 00:05:44.489
"There's the goose!"

110
00:05:44.849 --> 00:05:45.309
he said.

111
00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.492
Jack snatched it up and hurried down the beanstalk.

112
00:05:52.424 --> 00:05:56.566
The giant ran to the beanstalk and started to climb down after Jack.

113
00:05:57.687 --> 00:06:01.429
But he was not as quick, so Jack reached the ground first.

114
00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.451
"Mom, Mom, quick!

115
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:05.832
Where is the ax?"

116
00:06:06.152 --> 00:06:06.672
he cried.

117
00:06:06.692 --> 00:06:08.753
"Jack, where have you been?

118
00:06:09.154 --> 00:06:11.975
You left the ax right here," said his mom.

119
00:06:12.716 --> 00:06:16.198
Jack grabbed the ax and started to cut down the beanstalk.

120
00:06:17.138 --> 00:06:20.100
The beanstalk swayed back and forth as he chopped.

121
00:06:21.856 --> 00:06:22.617
"Oh no!

122
00:06:23.177 --> 00:06:25.599
The beanstalk is going to fall!"

123
00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:26.861
cried the giant.

124
00:06:27.841 --> 00:06:30.183
The giant held on as long as he could.

125
00:06:30.984 --> 00:06:35.588
But soon he lost his grip and fell all the way down and died.

126
00:06:35.608 --> 00:06:40.152
"Jack, what's going on here?"

127
00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:41.393
asked his mom.

128
00:06:41.413 --> 00:06:45.276
"Mom, I climbed up to the top of the beanstalk.

129
00:06:45.756 --> 00:06:47.078
Look what I found there.

130
00:06:47.578 --> 00:06:49.640
This goose lays golden eggs!"

131
00:06:51.292 --> 00:06:53.594
"Really? That's hard to believe!"

132
00:06:53.614 --> 00:06:54.995
"Just watch!

133
00:06:55.595 --> 00:06:56.436
Lay some eggs!"

134
00:06:56.776 --> 00:06:57.637
he told the goose.

135
00:06:58.337 --> 00:07:02.401
When his mother saw the large golden eggs, she was very pleased.

136
00:07:03.261 --> 00:07:04.682
"Oh my goodness!"

137
00:07:06.364 --> 00:07:11.547
After that, Jack and his mother were rich, and they were never hungry again.
